CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ base and member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/7, [dcl.init.general]/9.1-9.2: an empty
mem-initializer `B()' value-initializes the base, and a class without a
user-provided default constructor is zero-initialized.
full_member_initialization skipped empty initializers of POD bases, so
the base stayed nondeterministic (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
